WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.510 --> 00:09.347
It's the Seika era, in the democratic country of Nipponia.

3
00:10.515 --> 00:13.218
A huge ruling party has held power for a long time.

4
00:14.319 --> 00:17.455
This once-rich country is now on the edge of a cliff.

5
00:18.056 --> 00:20.325
The gap between rich and poor keeps growing.

6
00:20.391 --> 00:22.527
Both blue-collar workers and yakuza have no money.

7
00:22.594 --> 00:24.596
Even thieves have no money to steal.

8
00:24.662 --> 00:27.765
I am Yayoi "Lupin" Kisaragi!

9
00:27.832 --> 00:31.536
This great thief's surname is Kisaragi, her given name is Yayoi.

10
00:31.603 --> 00:35.807
She's after the Cabinet secret funds in Nagatanicho,

11
00:35.874 --> 00:37.509
the center of the nation.

12
00:37.575 --> 00:41.246
In the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office, there is a big safe.

13
00:41.813 --> 00:43.815
It's full of money.

14
00:43.882 --> 00:45.917
It's the Cabinet's secret stash.

15
00:45.984 --> 00:50.188
It's used to buy top-secret info, both at home and abroad.

16
00:50.255 --> 00:53.091
So no receipts are needed,

17
00:53.158 --> 00:55.960
and they don't have to report how it was used.

18
00:56.027 --> 00:57.729
I found my treasure!

19
00:57.795 --> 01:00.498
To get into Nagatanicho,

20
01:00.565 --> 01:03.368
Yayoi recruited a mysterious information broker, Inui.

21
01:03.434 --> 01:07.138
Then she approached Miyabi, daughter of Shiro Kobayakawa,

22
01:07.205 --> 01:10.675
heiress of the glorious political Kobayakawa family!

23
01:10.742 --> 01:13.578
I will become a Diet Member!

24
01:13.645 --> 01:17.615
Miyabi runs in the new Chiba District 17,

25
01:17.682 --> 01:20.084
which was split from the Kobayakawa home base.

26
01:20.151 --> 01:22.820
Her opponent is her own brother, Hayate.

27
01:22.887 --> 01:24.889
A battle between siblings!

28
01:24.956 --> 01:27.725
I can't believe they really dissolved it.

29
01:27.792 --> 01:29.928
I can't take this anymore!

30
01:29.994 --> 01:31.863
This is Masakado Natsume,

31
01:31.930 --> 01:34.199
the party's treasurer and a member of the Upper House.

32
01:34.265 --> 01:36.434
Hayate has no election experience.

33
01:36.501 --> 01:38.770
Your support would be reassuring.

34
01:38.836 --> 01:40.038
I would be glad to help.

35
01:40.104 --> 01:43.474
Are you perhaps interested in me?

36
01:43.541 --> 01:44.776
Yes, I am.

37
01:45.343 --> 01:48.947
Oh, I'm happy.

38
01:49.514 --> 01:51.983
A silly battle between two sly foxes has begun!

39
01:52.617 --> 01:56.921
What she will steal is the dark money of politicians!

40
01:56.988 --> 01:58.556
PoliticaLupin!

41
02:02.093 --> 02:04.629
FOR SALE

42
02:04.696 --> 02:05.897
What's this?

43
02:05.964 --> 02:07.665
Remains of dreams.

44
02:07.732 --> 02:10.268
The Jumbo lottery. Every time, I buy 30 tickets.

45
02:10.335 --> 02:13.871
For the past 20 years, I've won 81,000 yen.

46
02:13.938 --> 02:17.041
That's a 91% loss.

47
02:17.108 --> 02:18.409
Basically thrown in a ditch!

48
02:18.476 --> 02:19.544
A money ditch!

49
02:19.611 --> 02:22.380
Listen. Elections are about base, signboard, and bag.

50
02:22.447 --> 02:23.781
The bag is money.

51
02:23.848 --> 02:27.018
The more money you have, the more likely your victory. That's reality.

52
02:28.119 --> 02:29.153
Here.

53
02:29.220 --> 02:32.523
If you get the ruling party's endorsement, like your brother,

54
02:32.590 --> 02:33.758
you get…

55
02:33.825 --> 02:35.393
JUMBO LOTTERY TICKETS

56
02:35.460 --> 02:37.528
…20 million yen from the party.

57
02:37.595 --> 02:40.465
Also, you get lots of party members, support groups,

58
02:40.531 --> 02:44.335
and over 100 volunteers to help you out.

59
02:44.869 --> 02:46.004
And what do we have?

60
02:48.206 --> 02:50.608
A few elites! What about funds?

61
02:52.310 --> 02:54.312
Here's what I scraped together.

62
02:55.313 --> 02:57.348
-Three million yen. -Really?

63
02:59.250 --> 03:01.319
That's just the deposit!

64
03:01.386 --> 03:02.720
I thought you were rich?

65
03:02.787 --> 03:04.889
My parents are. I have no cash.

66
03:04.956 --> 03:06.391
We have no time! Let's take some photos!

67
03:06.457 --> 03:07.458
All right.

68
03:07.525 --> 03:10.962
Nice! Lovely! Perfect!

69
03:11.029 --> 03:14.032
Turn your body a little. Face the front.

70
03:14.098 --> 03:15.066
Excuse me.

71
03:15.133 --> 03:16.968
-Stay still. -A little more this way. Okay.

72
03:17.035 --> 03:19.137
Open up the chest a little.

73
03:19.203 --> 03:21.606
Relax! And now smile.

74
03:21.673 --> 03:24.575
Okay, smile!

75
03:24.642 --> 03:25.810
-Great! -Three!

76
03:25.877 --> 03:27.712
Two! One!

77
03:30.648 --> 03:31.616
HAYATE KOBAYAKAWA

78
03:36.154 --> 03:39.457
The Kokuji Party's endorsed candidate, Hayate Kobayakawa!

79
03:39.524 --> 03:41.592
Hayate Kobayakawa, everyone!

80
03:42.427 --> 03:45.797
A new wind for the Kokuji Party, Hayate Kobayakawa!

81
03:45.863 --> 03:49.767
Hayate Kobayakawa, everyone! Thank you!

82
03:49.834 --> 03:52.770
Please support Hayate Kobayakawa!

83
03:52.837 --> 03:53.738
HAYATE KOBAYAKAWA

84
03:53.805 --> 03:55.073
-Please support us. -Thank you!

85
03:55.139 --> 03:56.941
Thank you. Excuse me.

86
03:58.076 --> 03:59.977
It's finally starting!

87
04:00.044 --> 04:02.380
That health insurance scandal…

88
04:02.447 --> 04:03.681
What's with that?

89
04:03.748 --> 04:05.583
It's certainly wrong.

90
04:05.650 --> 04:08.920
If I'm elected, I'll change the Kokuji party from the inside.

91
04:08.986 --> 04:10.221
Good luck.

92
04:10.955 --> 04:12.590
-Do your best. -Thank you.

93
04:12.657 --> 04:13.791
I'll do all I can.

94
04:14.292 --> 04:16.361
KOKUJI PARTY

95
04:16.427 --> 04:19.630
We won't give my daughter any campaign money.

96
04:19.697 --> 04:21.699
Once she's a candidate,

97
04:21.766 --> 04:23.267
she's our enemy.

98
04:26.003 --> 04:28.740
The Chiba Shinyo Bank called.

99
04:28.806 --> 04:32.176
Your family home is being taken as collateral.

100
04:32.243 --> 04:33.177
What?

101
04:33.244 --> 04:36.881
Miyabi did it to raise campaign funds.

102
04:38.316 --> 04:40.485
That's our home base!

103
04:42.453 --> 04:45.556
If you lose, you lose both the house and land?

104
04:45.623 --> 04:46.758
Are you fine with that?

105
04:46.824 --> 04:47.925
Sure.

106
04:48.493 --> 04:51.562
My grandmother left this house to me.

107
04:55.833 --> 04:56.934
Come in.

108
04:57.568 --> 05:01.139
-Excuse me… -So huge…

109
05:01.205 --> 05:02.373
What…

110
05:02.940 --> 05:06.310
Mr. Hayate Kobayakawa is sure to become a politician

111
05:06.377 --> 05:08.780
who leads Japan's new era!

112
05:13.418 --> 05:15.720
He was raised by Mr. Shiro,

113
05:15.787 --> 05:19.357
and loves everyone here in Chiba District 17!

114
05:19.424 --> 05:21.859
Do your best!

115
05:21.926 --> 05:25.430
I think we can do a few more campaign tours.

116
05:25.997 --> 05:29.333
I don't think we need to cram in that many.

117
05:30.601 --> 05:32.537
Did the election planner, Mr. Hayashi, say that?

118
05:32.603 --> 05:34.205
No. It's my opinion.

119
05:36.340 --> 05:38.476
Oh, can we stop by my family home?

120
05:38.543 --> 05:39.544
We don't have time.

121
05:39.610 --> 05:40.578
Just a moment…

122
05:43.748 --> 05:44.749
Stop the car!

123
05:51.589 --> 05:54.091
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA

124
05:58.062 --> 05:59.230
Miyabi!

125
06:00.765 --> 06:04.669
What are you doing? Put your office somewhere else!

126
06:04.735 --> 06:05.670
Why?

127
06:05.736 --> 06:07.972
If you do this, then I can't stay here!

128
06:08.039 --> 06:09.240
Just stay at a hotel.

129
06:09.307 --> 06:10.508
Why should I?

130
06:10.575 --> 06:11.809
This is my house.

131
06:11.876 --> 06:13.311
That's only on paper.

132
06:13.377 --> 06:14.745
Paper is everything.

133
06:14.812 --> 06:15.847
Shall I make tea?

134
06:15.913 --> 06:17.381
-No, thanks. -No need.

135
06:17.448 --> 06:18.649
Hello.

136
06:18.716 --> 06:19.550
Hello.

137
06:19.617 --> 06:20.685
Hello.

138
06:21.752 --> 06:24.789
I didn't think you would use Mr. Shiro's family home as an election office.

139
06:24.856 --> 06:26.324
Can't you tell?

140
06:26.390 --> 06:28.226
Miyabi is the heiress, it seems.

141
06:28.292 --> 06:30.294
It's for saving money. We had no choice.

142
06:30.361 --> 06:31.462
Who's the strategist?

143
06:31.529 --> 06:32.730
Me.

144
06:38.169 --> 06:39.904
Appealing to the common people?

145
06:41.072 --> 06:43.508
A weak independent candidate with no party backing

146
06:43.574 --> 06:45.877
needs a desperate measure like this.

147
06:48.012 --> 06:51.082
When the Kobayakawa siblings fight in this election,

148
06:51.148 --> 06:52.350
the media will bite.

149
06:52.416 --> 06:54.919
It's like… an election hack.

150
06:59.023 --> 07:00.091
Do you think you can win?

151
07:02.426 --> 07:03.895
I don't know.

152
07:03.961 --> 07:07.832
The sibling fight is only good for making the first impact.

153
07:07.899 --> 07:10.001
We need a story.

154
07:10.067 --> 07:11.302
For example?

155
07:12.169 --> 07:15.306
"The little sister used to be bullied by her brother."

156
07:15.373 --> 07:17.074
Do you think we can win with that?

157
07:17.141 --> 07:19.510
Voters like strength and intelligence,

158
07:19.577 --> 07:21.646
but Miyabi has neither.

159
07:21.712 --> 07:24.181
She has approachability. So we need a story.

160
07:24.248 --> 07:26.684
One that would make everyone want to vote for her.

161
07:27.685 --> 07:33.257
A poor little girl who bravely opposes her bigwig father and brother.

162
07:37.128 --> 07:38.396
I don't like that.

163
07:38.462 --> 07:39.664
Don't be picky.

164
07:39.730 --> 07:40.798
It's too dark!

165
07:40.865 --> 07:42.900
Don't say it as if I'm the dark one.

166
07:46.370 --> 07:49.440
How about, "Pitiful but in a healthy way"?

167
07:52.009 --> 07:53.077
Hello!

168
07:53.144 --> 07:56.347
This is new candidate Miyabi Kobayakawa.

169
07:56.414 --> 07:57.248
Hello.

170
07:57.315 --> 07:59.817
She's running for the House of Representatives.

171
07:59.884 --> 08:01.986
Miyabi Kobayakawa!

172
08:02.053 --> 08:03.254
Hello.

173
08:03.321 --> 08:05.323
Please support her!

174
08:05.389 --> 08:08.125
-Found a board! -Yeah.

175
08:10.461 --> 08:11.395
All right.

176
08:11.462 --> 08:13.230
-I'll put it up. -Yeah.

177
08:13.297 --> 08:14.732
Okay.

178
08:18.302 --> 08:19.937
TO CREATE FAIR POLITICS WITH NO COLLUSION!

179
08:24.976 --> 08:27.044
Sorry for making a ruckus. Hello.

180
08:27.111 --> 08:29.013
-Please support us. -Please.

181
08:29.080 --> 08:30.181
It's so hot!

182
08:30.781 --> 08:32.049
Drink some water.

183
08:32.116 --> 08:33.050
Thank you!

184
08:33.718 --> 08:36.487
Hello! I'm Miyabi Kobayakawa.

185
08:36.554 --> 08:37.521
Hello.

186
08:42.693 --> 08:43.894
All right.

187
08:43.961 --> 08:46.831
-Please support us. -Okay.

188
08:47.765 --> 08:50.901
Miyabi Kobayakawa is putting up posters!

189
08:50.968 --> 08:52.269
The person herself!

190
08:52.336 --> 08:53.270
Hello.

191
08:53.337 --> 08:55.072
Please support us!

192
08:55.139 --> 08:56.841
-Do your best! -Thank you!

193
08:56.907 --> 08:58.643
-I'm rooting for you! -Do your best!

194
08:58.709 --> 08:59.677
Please support us.

195
08:59.744 --> 09:02.947
Miyabi Kobayakawa is putting up posters!

196
09:03.014 --> 09:04.915
Please support us!

197
09:04.982 --> 09:05.916
Okay.

198
09:06.417 --> 09:08.853
TEN DAYS UNTIL VOTING DAY

199
09:15.693 --> 09:17.695
DISTRICT 17 - MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA INDEPENDENT

200
09:17.762 --> 09:18.863
I'M PUTTING UP POSTERS

201
09:18.929 --> 09:21.732
I have no campaign funds, so I borrowed money.

202
09:21.799 --> 09:25.503
I have no car, so I run and put up posters along the way.

203
09:26.037 --> 09:28.873
I have decent stamina. Please support me!

204
09:28.939 --> 09:30.107
I'm off!

205
09:30.174 --> 09:31.475
IS THIS A PUNISHMENT GAME?

206
09:31.542 --> 09:33.210
THE ELECTION WILL BE OVER BY THE TIME SHE'S DONE

207
09:33.277 --> 09:34.445
BOTH CUTE AND PITIFUL

208
09:34.512 --> 09:35.513
Let's go!

209
09:35.579 --> 09:38.449
-Thank you! -Thank you so much!

210
09:38.516 --> 09:40.785
-In this heat… -Impressive!

211
09:43.087 --> 09:44.522
Okay.

212
09:44.588 --> 09:46.490
-Please drink this. -Thank you!

213
09:46.557 --> 09:47.625
Thank you.

214
09:47.692 --> 09:50.461
Back then, you used to attend Mr. Ichiro and Mr. Shiro's speeches, right?

215
09:50.528 --> 09:51.362
Yes!

216
09:51.429 --> 09:52.697
How you've grown!

217
09:52.763 --> 09:53.998
I'm 166 cm.

218
09:54.832 --> 09:57.001
-Good luck. -Thank you!

219
09:57.068 --> 09:59.670
-I'll do my best. -Thank you.

220
09:59.737 --> 10:01.172
Miyabi Kobayakawa!

221
10:01.238 --> 10:02.239
Please support us!

222
10:02.306 --> 10:04.475
A new wind for the Kokuji Party,

223
10:04.542 --> 10:07.411
endorsed candidate Hayate Kobayakawa!

224
10:07.478 --> 10:11.315
Hayate Kobayakawa! Thank you!

225
10:11.382 --> 10:14.118
Sorry for the loud mic behind you.

226
10:14.185 --> 10:17.955
We wish candidate Miyabi Kobayakawa good luck.

227
10:18.556 --> 10:20.524
A new wind for the Kokuji Party,

228
10:20.591 --> 10:23.494
endorsed candidate Hayate Kobayakawa!

229
10:23.561 --> 10:27.164
Hayate Kobayakawa! Thank you!

230
10:27.231 --> 10:29.633
Sorry for the loud mic behind you.

231
10:29.700 --> 10:31.435
-So hot. -Welcome back.

232
10:31.502 --> 10:32.336
Welcome back.

233
10:32.403 --> 10:33.237
Thank you.

234
10:33.304 --> 10:34.872
Welcome back.

235
10:34.939 --> 10:36.574
Hey. You're back early.

236
10:38.409 --> 10:40.044
I cut it short.

237
10:40.678 --> 10:42.646
It's so hot…

238
10:48.586 --> 10:51.522
You should do more stationary speeches.

239
10:52.123 --> 10:53.390
No way…

240
10:54.358 --> 10:57.161
People will have to stand in the heat and listen.

241
10:59.330 --> 11:01.265
I'll win either way.

242
11:05.035 --> 11:08.072
CANDIDATE SUPPORT RATES

243
11:08.139 --> 11:11.242
HAYATE - 41% SUPPORT MIYABI - 19% SUPPORT

244
11:20.851 --> 11:22.353
Excuse me.

245
11:22.920 --> 11:23.821
Yes?

246
11:25.356 --> 11:26.257
Yes?

247
11:26.824 --> 11:29.393
Hey, may we help you put up posters?

248
11:29.460 --> 11:31.195
-Are you sure? -Yes!

249
11:31.262 --> 11:32.229
Thank you!

250
11:32.296 --> 11:35.132
People often say "taking over the family business,"

251
11:35.199 --> 11:37.568
but is politics a family business?

252
11:37.635 --> 11:40.070
It concerns the whole country, after all.

253
11:40.137 --> 11:44.809
Nipponia is a parliamentary democracy with no class system.

254
11:44.875 --> 11:45.743
Supposedly.

255
11:45.810 --> 11:46.811
But…

256
11:46.877 --> 11:50.247
But there is still hierarchy between people, isn't there?

257
11:50.314 --> 11:52.550
Hereditary succession is like that.

258
11:52.616 --> 11:55.452
The posters and map are inside. Thank you so much.

259
11:55.519 --> 11:58.522
-Thank you! -We're off!

260
11:58.589 --> 12:00.057
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA

261
12:00.124 --> 12:01.292
Momo!

262
12:01.358 --> 12:02.827
You're doing well!

263
12:02.893 --> 12:03.861
You came here to see me?

264
12:03.928 --> 12:06.997
After seeing Miyabi running out there, I couldn't sit still!

265
12:07.064 --> 12:09.600
Yeah, she is like a celeb now.

266
12:09.667 --> 12:11.335
-Come in! -Sure.

267
12:11.402 --> 12:12.937
I'm Saibara.

268
12:13.003 --> 12:16.440
This program brings together candidates from a district gathering attention,

269
12:16.507 --> 12:18.142
and we're live again today.

270
12:18.209 --> 12:20.945
District 17 is a hot topic, because of the sibling rivalry.

271
12:22.112 --> 12:24.548
The man in the middle, Mr. Hachimaki, is also independent.

272
12:24.615 --> 12:27.785
The opposition parties didn't even field candidates here,

273
12:27.852 --> 12:30.788
because this is called the "Kobayakawa Kingdom."

274
12:30.855 --> 12:32.957
Anyone but the Kokuji Party is a sure loser here.

275
12:34.258 --> 12:36.927
Miyabi, why do you run in District 17?

276
12:38.362 --> 12:41.098
I lived here with my grandparents until middle school.

277
12:41.932 --> 12:45.502
Your pledge is to abolish hereditary politics,

278
12:45.569 --> 12:49.206
but running in the Kobayakawa Kingdom is close to inheriting, isn't it?

279
12:49.273 --> 12:53.110
I'm not getting any support from my father or the party.

280
12:53.677 --> 12:55.913
But you're a politician's child.

281
12:55.980 --> 13:00.150
It's not that politicians' children must not become politicians.

282
13:00.217 --> 13:04.788
It's unfair that children automatically inherit a base,

283
13:04.855 --> 13:06.891
and that this has become normal.

284
13:06.957 --> 13:08.893
As such, it must be abolished.

285
13:08.959 --> 13:13.230
Of course, everyone can choose to run for elections if they want to.

286
13:13.864 --> 13:17.067
Hayate, you inherited the base. Your response?

287
13:17.134 --> 13:19.603
I'm not sure this is a response,

288
13:20.170 --> 13:24.108
but however much she acts like a commoner, my sister is a Kobayakawa.

289
13:24.174 --> 13:27.778
She even ran around on the streets just to garner popularity.

290
13:27.845 --> 13:29.380
She's pretending to be common folk.

291
13:29.446 --> 13:31.382
It's worse because she hides it.

292
13:31.448 --> 13:35.753
She's part of the class system that she herself wants to abolish.

293
13:35.819 --> 13:38.389
You sound harsh. Are you on bad terms?

294
13:38.455 --> 13:39.323
Not at all.

295
13:39.390 --> 13:43.594
No. Back then, she was adorable and followed me around.

296
13:43.661 --> 13:46.430
She cried saying that studying was hard,

297
13:46.497 --> 13:48.465
and I taught her each time.

298
13:49.233 --> 13:51.535
Well, she's a girl, after all.

299
13:51.602 --> 13:53.804
Girls are allowed to be that spoiled.

300
13:55.973 --> 13:59.810
Bro, in high school, you came crying to me, too.

301
13:59.877 --> 14:02.112
"I might have gotten my girlfriend pregnant, what do I do?"

302
14:02.179 --> 14:06.150
It shocked me that you and Dad only talked about how to hide it,

303
14:06.216 --> 14:08.352
not worrying about the girl.

304
14:08.419 --> 14:10.821
She wasn't pregnant in the end, but…

305
14:10.888 --> 14:14.158
You were in the news for causing trouble at a host club!

306
14:14.224 --> 14:15.759
Who cleaned that up?

307
14:15.826 --> 14:16.894
I didn't ask you to.

308
14:16.961 --> 14:19.263
You got drunk, vomited on the street, and got photographed.

309
14:19.330 --> 14:20.798
People puke, you know.

310
14:20.864 --> 14:23.167
-Don't say "puke." -You brought it up first!

311
14:23.233 --> 14:24.568
No, I didn't say "puke."

312
14:24.635 --> 14:25.669
You just did.

313
14:27.171 --> 14:28.105
Maybe emesis?

314
14:29.306 --> 14:32.176
Emesis? Why are you getting all medical here?

315
14:36.380 --> 14:37.681
You two are in sync.

316
14:37.748 --> 14:39.316
-No, we're not! -No, we're not!

317
14:40.684 --> 14:43.654
Let's end the sibling talk

318
14:43.721 --> 14:46.423
and move on to each of your policies.

319
14:46.490 --> 14:49.059
Who would like to go first?

320
14:49.126 --> 14:50.761
It's so over.

321
14:50.828 --> 14:53.664
They both look good on video.

322
14:57.634 --> 14:59.636
It's your fault for saying unnecessary things.

323
14:59.703 --> 15:01.605
You were annoying too.

324
15:01.672 --> 15:03.540
You were pretty mean.

325
15:03.607 --> 15:05.342
True, he was unprofessional.

326
15:05.409 --> 15:07.411
Natsume, you're on her side?

327
15:07.478 --> 15:09.947
That was not an attitude you should use in formal events.

328
15:10.447 --> 15:13.984
It's weird that I have to debate my sister in the first place.

329
15:14.051 --> 15:18.322
Why do you have to run in my district? Run somewhere else.

330
15:19.223 --> 15:21.525
Do you hold a grudge against me?

331
15:24.628 --> 15:26.997
You cried in your third year of middle school.

332
15:27.898 --> 15:30.401
Before summer vacation, your grades dropped.

333
15:30.467 --> 15:33.137
Dad said that you had promised to study,

334
15:33.203 --> 15:35.272
and made you throw out your things.

335
15:51.255 --> 15:54.725
I can't forget it. That was cruel.

336
15:55.993 --> 15:58.695
You don't have to listen to Dad, you know?

337
16:03.000 --> 16:05.736
I remember the time you cried too.

338
16:07.171 --> 16:10.074
ROUSSEAU THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

339
16:27.424 --> 16:28.992
What is Miyabi doing?

340
16:29.059 --> 16:31.161
She doesn't even help around the house!

341
16:37.000 --> 16:38.735
Hey, Grandma, listen.

342
16:39.603 --> 16:42.339
"Man is born free,

343
16:42.406 --> 16:45.676
but everywhere he is in chains."

344
16:45.742 --> 16:47.010
Deep, right?

345
16:48.545 --> 16:52.249
To stay free, we need a social contract.

346
16:52.316 --> 16:54.418
This idea of popular sovereignty

347
16:54.485 --> 16:56.820
led to our Constitution.

348
16:59.189 --> 17:01.325
JEAN-JACQUES ROUSSEAU THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

349
17:03.594 --> 17:05.262
You don't have to read this.

350
17:08.799 --> 17:10.801
I want to be a politician.

351
17:10.868 --> 17:14.171
A job to improve the country. It sounds fun.

352
17:14.238 --> 17:17.508
And if I take over the family business, big bro can make games.

353
17:19.543 --> 17:20.611
Listen, Miyabi.

354
17:21.245 --> 17:23.981
Your grandfather and father

355
17:24.748 --> 17:27.951
dislike women who become politicians.

356
17:28.519 --> 17:29.987
You understand?

357
17:38.028 --> 17:39.830
If only our positions were reversed…

358
17:41.498 --> 17:42.666
That's what I thought.

359
17:44.968 --> 17:48.372
Don't mind me, but give up trying to beat the Kobayakawa family.

360
17:48.438 --> 17:52.576
You'll lose. We have money and people behind us.

361
17:52.643 --> 17:54.378
-Hayate. -I have to be blunt!

362
17:54.444 --> 17:55.546
She understands nothing.

363
18:02.452 --> 18:08.725
The head of my law office is elderly, and he retired

364
18:08.792 --> 18:10.561
and closed down the law firm.

365
18:10.627 --> 18:15.399
So I decided to run in the elections, to change society through law.

366
18:16.300 --> 18:20.204
I was just on an online talkshow,

367
18:20.837 --> 18:23.440
but I couldn't say anything.

368
18:23.507 --> 18:26.343
INDEPENDENT HACHIMAKI

369
18:26.410 --> 18:29.680
I couldn't say anything at all.

370
18:29.746 --> 18:31.014
You'll be fine!

371
18:31.081 --> 18:32.182
Do your best!

372
18:32.249 --> 18:34.384
Thank you! I'll do all I can.

373
18:37.454 --> 18:38.956
Before the campaign,

374
18:40.557 --> 18:41.792
Mr. Kiuchi came by.

375
18:42.659 --> 18:44.561
I got Suzuran hamburger rice crackers.

376
18:44.628 --> 18:45.996
Hamburger crackers?

377
18:46.063 --> 18:48.565
They are a long-time supporter of Mr. Shiro's.

378
18:49.700 --> 18:51.868
Did you come all this way to see me?

379
18:51.935 --> 18:55.272
Well, it's work. I have to give all prefectural party members…

380
18:56.139 --> 18:57.574
Our "seasonal greeting."

381
18:57.641 --> 19:00.244
A "seasonal greeting"?

382
19:00.911 --> 19:02.112
What is that?

383
19:06.216 --> 19:08.252
What? Is something wrong?

384
19:09.052 --> 19:11.788
Please tell me. I want to learn everything.

385
19:12.856 --> 19:16.693
This is our seasonal greeting. Thank you.

386
19:17.261 --> 19:19.796
Thank you. Thank you.

387
19:19.863 --> 19:23.800
I heard from Kiuchi. Hayate got angry?

388
19:23.867 --> 19:25.669
Not really angry…

389
19:27.437 --> 19:29.906
More like shocked.

390
19:30.407 --> 19:34.278
In an election race, money flies in stacks of cash.

391
19:35.479 --> 19:37.381
That's just how things work.

392
19:38.215 --> 19:39.850
Sorry to ask, Natsume…

393
19:39.916 --> 19:40.984
Yes?

394
19:41.051 --> 19:43.120
Please talk some sense into him.

395
20:03.607 --> 20:05.008
In elections, we need

396
20:05.642 --> 20:08.945
support from prefectural and city assembly members.

397
20:09.012 --> 20:11.715
They ask local companies and residents

398
20:11.782 --> 20:15.786
to vote for you and gather the votes.

399
20:15.852 --> 20:19.222
And this is the "reward."

400
20:19.289 --> 20:20.624
That's election fraud, isn't it?

401
20:21.858 --> 20:23.894
True, you can't do it during the election itself.

402
20:23.960 --> 20:26.129
Even before the election it's still fraud.

403
20:26.196 --> 20:28.065
It's only fraud if you say "Vote for me."

404
20:28.131 --> 20:30.867
It's just "thanks for your help" and giving them cash?

405
20:30.934 --> 20:32.536
That's what's going on, right?

406
20:32.602 --> 20:34.471
Neither side says anything.

407
20:35.405 --> 20:37.507
It's an unspoken understanding, so it isn't fraud.

408
20:37.574 --> 20:39.176
-But that's… -But that's…

409
20:39.676 --> 20:40.577
It's wrong.

410
20:41.378 --> 20:42.579
I said so too.

411
20:42.646 --> 20:45.315
What if I were to expose that, like what I did today?

412
20:45.382 --> 20:46.917
You've got no proof!

413
20:47.984 --> 20:49.653
Even I saw nothing.

414
20:50.520 --> 20:52.622
No one will admit they received any money.

415
20:53.223 --> 20:56.026
And we won't say, "We gave them money" either.

416
20:56.593 --> 20:58.895
Is that how you became a Diet member, Mr. Natsume?

417
21:03.633 --> 21:05.302
Luckily for me,

418
21:07.137 --> 21:10.474
a retiring senior member recommended me,

419
21:10.540 --> 21:12.776
so I got his supporters.

420
21:12.843 --> 21:16.213
It wasn't a tough fight, so there was no money to hand out.

421
21:16.279 --> 21:20.684
I was lucky to get the endorsement.

422
21:20.751 --> 21:23.320
Not every election depends on money.

423
21:23.387 --> 21:25.956
But in my District 17, money was being handed out.

424
21:27.224 --> 21:28.725
If it was you, Mr. Natsume,

425
21:29.292 --> 21:30.927
would you just quietly go along?

426
21:32.362 --> 21:36.900
I'm not going to be Prime Minister. I just hold a small seat.

427
21:38.068 --> 21:42.139
I can't imagine what it's like to be in your position.

428
21:46.710 --> 21:48.445
In the end,

429
21:49.780 --> 21:51.214
you must decide for yourself.

430
21:59.890 --> 22:02.793
It's hard being a Diet member.

431
22:03.360 --> 22:04.728
What do you mean?

432
22:05.762 --> 22:08.365
The money being handed out.

433
22:10.834 --> 22:12.469
I mean, I don't blame you.

434
22:13.003 --> 22:15.238
That's how the world is nowadays.

435
22:15.739 --> 22:19.609
Is that money party grants? Donations?

436
22:19.676 --> 22:21.044
Or… Cabinet secret funds?

437
22:22.646 --> 22:24.481
Well, it's probably dirty money, anyway.

438
22:24.548 --> 22:28.585
With all due respect, it's not necessarily dirty money.

439
22:30.620 --> 22:33.256
If the party branch issues a receipt

440
22:33.323 --> 22:37.427
and the member records it as a donation in the political funds report, it's legal.

441
22:37.494 --> 22:39.362
Did you issue a receipt?

442
22:40.430 --> 22:42.032
When you're about to be exposed,

443
22:42.098 --> 22:44.968
you issue a receipt after the fact and record it.

444
22:45.035 --> 22:47.170
The report is released over a year later.

445
22:47.237 --> 22:49.306
The election will be long over then.

446
22:50.307 --> 22:54.277
That's a very convenient rule!

447
22:58.615 --> 22:59.616
Excuse me.

448
23:02.619 --> 23:05.589
Wow, you're so good at this!

449
23:06.156 --> 23:07.190
Thank you!

450
23:13.930 --> 23:15.832
Everyone, I'm sorry.

451
23:17.400 --> 23:20.303
You all worked hard with me, but I…

452
23:22.038 --> 23:23.440
Clumsy me!

453
23:23.507 --> 23:26.076
It's because of the heat! This summer is so hot!

454
23:26.643 --> 23:28.879
We're done for today. See you tomorrow.

455
23:28.945 --> 23:31.248
Thank you for today.

456
23:31.314 --> 23:33.350
See you tomorrow. Take care.

457
23:33.416 --> 23:34.317
See you.

458
23:34.384 --> 23:35.986
-Thank you! -Thank you very much.

459
23:36.052 --> 23:37.621
Be careful on the way home!

460
23:37.687 --> 23:39.556
Thank you for today. Please take care.

461
23:39.623 --> 23:40.891
Good work.

462
23:40.957 --> 23:43.493
-We're going home already? -Why?

463
23:43.560 --> 23:45.395
What's wrong?

464
23:45.462 --> 23:47.097
Getting sick of each other?

465
23:47.163 --> 23:49.466
Why are you here all of a sudden?

466
23:50.433 --> 23:53.169
You went viral. In a bad way.

467
23:53.737 --> 23:54.804
Huh?

468
23:57.741 --> 23:59.609
I'm running in this election!

469
24:00.310 --> 24:03.380
Everything is because of summer!

470
24:04.614 --> 24:06.483
People puke, you know.

471
24:06.550 --> 24:08.318
Don't say "puke."

472
24:08.385 --> 24:09.319
SPENT TONS OF MONEY ON A HOST, THEN GOT DUMPED

473
24:09.386 --> 24:10.754
GETTING DRUNK AND VOMITING

474
24:11.454 --> 24:13.256
IDIOT DAUGHTER OF THE KOBAYAKAWAS

475
24:13.323 --> 24:14.424
STUPID SPOILED GIRL

476
24:14.491 --> 24:15.725
NO CURE FOR STUPIDITY

477
24:15.792 --> 24:17.961
STUPID WOMAN

478
24:18.028 --> 24:19.629
I HATE POLITICIANS LIKE THIS

479
24:24.501 --> 24:26.903
Don't read this stuff. It will poison your mind.

480
24:29.039 --> 24:31.875
Your brother's talk was awful too.

481
24:31.942 --> 24:33.977
-True. -Right?

482
24:34.044 --> 24:37.213
But his side has an ad agency handling the internet.

483
24:37.280 --> 24:40.116
How much are they spending? Is there a spending cap?

484
24:40.183 --> 24:41.151
No.

485
24:41.217 --> 24:42.385
Why?

486
24:42.452 --> 24:45.055
I tried, but it was pointless.

487
24:46.590 --> 24:47.691
I feel stupid.

488
24:49.159 --> 24:51.628
Well, I'm a stupid woman, so it's natural.

489
24:53.330 --> 24:56.600
In the end, it's all about money. How frustrating.

490
24:59.202 --> 25:01.571
Yes, it's all about money.

491
25:02.272 --> 25:04.107
The world runs on money.

492
25:05.508 --> 25:07.978
Don't get scared just because some people mocked you.

493
25:08.044 --> 25:10.180
Don't be whining just yet.

494
25:11.648 --> 25:14.317
You mortgaged this house and borrowed money.

495
25:14.384 --> 25:16.019
That's a great resolve.

496
25:17.387 --> 25:18.622
But is it?

497
25:19.723 --> 25:22.626
If you lose, your dad will just handle it.

498
25:22.692 --> 25:24.127
He'll help.

499
25:24.194 --> 25:27.197
He won't let this home base of his be taken by the bank.

500
25:27.263 --> 25:29.032
You know that, right?

501
25:29.733 --> 25:33.003
You haven't thrown anything anyway.

502
25:33.069 --> 25:34.804
You have everything.

503
25:34.871 --> 25:38.675
Your brother was right. You're a spoiled girl who has it all.

504
25:41.044 --> 25:42.178
But…

505
25:42.746 --> 25:45.315
what about the people who helped put up posters?

506
25:46.016 --> 25:48.051
They didn't get a single yen.

507
25:48.718 --> 25:51.955
They came because they wanted to support you. What about them?

508
25:52.622 --> 25:55.191
Will you throw them away? Will you quit?

509
25:59.396 --> 26:03.099
No one here has money on their mind.

510
26:14.110 --> 26:15.378
No one here has money on their mind!

511
26:16.413 --> 26:18.682
I'm not after Miyabi's money.

512
26:19.816 --> 26:21.418
Look who's talking. A thief.

513
26:21.484 --> 26:23.453
-I'm a great thief. -Great!

514
26:30.493 --> 26:32.362
No need to worry.

515
26:32.429 --> 26:35.932
If you hear that the opponent is giving out money behind the scenes,

516
26:35.999 --> 26:37.467
you would lose confidence.

517
26:37.534 --> 26:39.202
They didn't give out any money.

518
26:39.269 --> 26:41.638
They absolutely did. I told you about it.

519
26:41.705 --> 26:44.207
The election starts before the official day of voting.

520
26:44.274 --> 26:45.575
Yes, I heard.

521
26:45.642 --> 26:48.978
Even before the start date, the battle has already begun.

522
26:51.014 --> 26:52.048
Let me hear it.

523
26:52.749 --> 26:55.685
There are districts you absolutely can't lose.

524
26:56.352 --> 26:59.322
Decisive districts. All parties will spend big money for them.

525
26:59.389 --> 27:00.490
I see…

526
27:00.557 --> 27:03.126
I got detailed info beforehand,

527
27:03.860 --> 27:06.529
so I worked before the start date.

528
27:07.831 --> 27:10.934
First, I had someone visit the Kokuji Party office

529
27:11.000 --> 27:13.236
and learn the schedule, pretending to file a petition.

530
27:14.270 --> 27:17.107
Wild boars are ruining my fields.

531
27:17.173 --> 27:18.975
A boar showed up the other day too…

532
27:19.042 --> 27:21.077
-Really? -Yeah. I fought it.

533
27:21.144 --> 27:22.912
They are strong!

534
27:22.979 --> 27:26.249
But I gave them the good ol' right hook!

535
27:26.316 --> 27:28.218
And was able to drive them back.

536
27:28.284 --> 27:31.154
And then with my pride, the "Left Straight",

537
27:31.221 --> 27:33.890
I made sure they didn't come back.

538
27:33.957 --> 27:36.559
If you install a right-turn signal at that intersection,

539
27:36.626 --> 27:38.027
there won't be any traffic jams.

540
27:38.094 --> 27:40.363
Then, you can sleep for ten more minutes.

541
27:40.430 --> 27:42.132
Please come check it out.

542
27:42.198 --> 27:44.667
When can you come? When are you free?

543
27:44.734 --> 27:46.636
-Well… -When is it?

544
27:46.703 --> 27:48.805
You are quite busy, I see.

545
27:49.372 --> 27:51.941
Every party member had the same schedule.

546
27:52.509 --> 27:54.677
And Kobayakawa staff have a rule.

547
27:54.744 --> 27:59.883
When they come to Chiba, they always eat at Suzuran Hamburg.

548
27:59.949 --> 28:01.050
SUZURAN HAMBURG AS USUAL

549
28:01.851 --> 28:03.186
So, an ambush.

550
28:06.289 --> 28:08.358
The secretary, Kiuchi, appears.

551
28:14.330 --> 28:15.665
Oh, sorry.

552
28:15.732 --> 28:16.866
It's okay.

553
29:03.313 --> 29:05.682
Welcome. Please choose any seat.

554
29:20.296 --> 29:21.898
Sir, is this yours?

555
29:22.599 --> 29:23.633
Right!

556
29:24.767 --> 29:25.935
Thank you.

557
29:52.128 --> 29:53.396
And so…

558
29:53.463 --> 29:56.799
the shady money disappeared.

559
29:58.034 --> 30:00.203
So what was handed out instead?

560
30:01.638 --> 30:03.406
Remains of dreams.

561
30:03.907 --> 30:06.943
I'm asking you, what are you talking about?

562
30:07.010 --> 30:09.746
I thought hard about it,

563
30:10.713 --> 30:14.517
but I don't know why they handed me this stuff.

564
30:15.518 --> 30:17.453
Old lottery tickets?

565
30:17.520 --> 30:21.224
If you're short of money, tell me!

566
30:21.291 --> 30:23.526
I have no idea what you are saying.

567
30:23.593 --> 30:25.295
Just spit it out already!

568
30:25.361 --> 30:26.429
I…

569
30:27.530 --> 30:30.133
I handed out the envelopes I got from the Secretary General.

570
30:32.902 --> 30:37.674
The party staff divided the cash in my room,

571
30:37.740 --> 30:40.109
and there was no problem then.

572
30:40.176 --> 30:43.813
The money vanished only in Chiba District 17.

573
30:43.880 --> 30:46.883
I did my job just as I always do!

574
30:46.950 --> 30:50.420
I didn't touch or look inside the envelopes.

575
30:51.988 --> 30:54.857
Someone posted on FaceNote…

576
30:54.924 --> 30:58.962
"Party leadership isn't supporting Kobayakawa Jr."

577
31:00.029 --> 31:03.433
"This is how they tell people not to vote for him."

578
31:03.933 --> 31:06.436
Such rumors are spreading.

579
31:06.502 --> 31:07.670
What a disaster!

580
31:07.737 --> 31:09.072
I'm sorry.

581
31:09.138 --> 31:11.140
-Did you do it? -I didn't, but…

582
31:11.874 --> 31:13.409
I'm sure it's my fault.

583
31:14.110 --> 31:16.779
I have no idea, but I'm sure…

584
31:18.281 --> 31:20.216
-Probably… -Which is it?

585
31:20.283 --> 31:23.086
Enough. Call Taniguchi.

586
31:23.152 --> 31:26.122
Explain it was a mix-up.

587
31:26.189 --> 31:29.392
Do we give the seasonal greetings again?

588
31:29.459 --> 31:30.526
Fool!

589
31:31.494 --> 31:34.364
We can't give out secret cash during the election.

590
31:34.430 --> 31:36.299
You'll have to beg them to help!

591
31:36.366 --> 31:37.767
I understand!

592
31:40.870 --> 31:43.306
Are you sure he didn't do it?

593
31:44.307 --> 31:45.975
That man is unable to tell lies.

594
31:46.042 --> 31:48.778
Then someone must have

595
31:48.845 --> 31:50.880
switched the contents somewhere.

596
31:53.082 --> 31:54.984
Who did it?

597
32:13.669 --> 32:15.605
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

598
32:31.320 --> 32:33.523
I saw heaven.

599
32:34.190 --> 32:36.025
That's too early.

600
32:36.092 --> 32:39.862
I wanted to see you in a wedding dress.

601
32:40.630 --> 32:43.099
Probably can't do that in this era.

602
32:44.534 --> 32:45.868
Yeah.

603
32:45.935 --> 32:49.338
You've been like this since you were small.

604
32:50.706 --> 32:54.477
This house is dear to me,

605
32:54.544 --> 32:55.912
but to you,

606
32:57.180 --> 32:59.682
it's like a chain.

607
33:02.251 --> 33:04.854
You only live once.

608
33:08.825 --> 33:10.226
I'll leave this house

609
33:10.293 --> 33:12.562
to you.

610
33:14.163 --> 33:17.967
You can even sell it. Do what you like.

611
33:23.473 --> 33:29.378
THE SOCIAL CONTRACT

612
33:48.731 --> 33:50.633
-What? You'll never hit. -It seems hard.

613
33:51.434 --> 33:53.102
-It's never a win. -Really?

614
33:53.970 --> 33:56.139
-I've never eaten this before. -Really?

615
33:56.205 --> 33:58.374
-I'm curious. -I always have this.

616
34:01.511 --> 34:03.379
Sorry about yesterday.

617
34:05.515 --> 34:09.552
I started this myself, knowing it would likely fail, but I lost my nerve.

618
34:13.055 --> 34:15.391
This was my Bible in middle school.

619
34:16.425 --> 34:19.495
Rousseau is a strange person with many odd points,

620
34:19.562 --> 34:21.664
but I liked that he didn't lie.

621
34:22.231 --> 34:24.534
I haven't opened it in 15 years, but I still remember a lot.

622
34:25.101 --> 34:27.770
You sure read hard books.

623
34:27.837 --> 34:31.040
Back then. Otherwise, I only read English study books.

624
34:31.741 --> 34:32.808
Like Murphy.

625
34:47.290 --> 34:50.326
Miyabi! Miyabi! Wait…

626
34:51.327 --> 34:53.663
You look super smart right now.

627
34:54.297 --> 34:55.164
What?

628
35:13.649 --> 35:16.018
Won't they say I'm showing off my English?

629
35:16.085 --> 35:18.054
Better than being thought of as a stupid woman!

630
35:29.665 --> 35:34.136
HER ENGLISH IS PRETTY NATURAL GOOD PRONUNCIATION

631
35:34.203 --> 35:35.371
Hello?

632
35:36.239 --> 35:39.175
If you're in Chiba right now, I have good material for you.

633
35:40.977 --> 35:42.178
A screenshot

634
35:42.945 --> 35:45.514
of a FaceNote post deleted last night.

635
35:46.015 --> 35:48.451
It seems it was deleted, but what is this?

636
35:48.517 --> 35:49.685
Nothing…

637
35:51.420 --> 35:53.522
Have there been bribery acts like this in the past?

638
35:54.957 --> 35:56.592
No, I really…

639
35:56.659 --> 35:58.594
This time I only got lottery tickets,

640
35:58.661 --> 36:00.730
and expired ones at that.

641
36:00.796 --> 36:01.964
Not cash vouchers.

642
36:02.031 --> 36:05.401
"Only" lottery tickets "this time."

643
36:06.769 --> 36:08.337
What about before?

644
36:08.404 --> 36:11.240
Elections are more favorable than you think

645
36:11.307 --> 36:13.409
when you have money.

646
36:13.476 --> 36:16.112
That's why old politics are being upheld.

647
36:16.178 --> 36:17.513
-Yeah! -That's right!

648
36:18.080 --> 36:20.716
We must change that system.

649
36:20.783 --> 36:22.084
Speak English!

650
36:22.151 --> 36:24.487
Can't you talk without a script?

651
36:39.435 --> 36:40.970
MIYABI SPEAKING ENGLISH

652
36:41.037 --> 36:43.973
MIYABI IS SO COOL SEEMS SHE'S ACTUALLY SMART?

653
36:44.040 --> 36:46.375
People don't exist for the sake of the nation…

654
36:49.578 --> 36:50.980
…nation for the people.

655
36:51.047 --> 36:54.283
Mr. Hachimaki also borrowed money to run, it seems.

656
36:55.618 --> 36:58.421
I listened to his speeches. He made some good points.

657
36:58.487 --> 36:59.789
I see.

658
36:59.855 --> 37:02.024
He doesn't stand out at all though.

659
37:03.059 --> 37:05.528
Because laws are insufficient,

660
37:05.594 --> 37:09.265
we often can't help people in trouble.

661
37:09.332 --> 37:13.002
Some people can't be helped unless we work on legislation.

662
37:13.069 --> 37:15.504
That's why I, a lawyer,

663
37:15.571 --> 37:17.206
chose to enter politics.

664
37:20.976 --> 37:21.911
Well…

665
37:23.079 --> 37:24.480
Let's talk policy.

666
37:24.547 --> 37:28.984
The Justice Ministry has a budget for rehabilitating offenders,

667
37:29.051 --> 37:32.355
but not for victims' mental care and supporting their daily lives.

668
37:32.421 --> 37:35.858
3 DAYS UNTIL VOTING

669
37:36.792 --> 37:38.761
Each of you

670
37:38.828 --> 37:41.664
has in yourself a desire to improve society,

671
37:41.731 --> 37:43.366
and we'll build a path together.

672
37:43.432 --> 37:44.533
That's an election.

673
37:46.235 --> 37:48.771
I want to smash, here and now,

674
37:48.838 --> 37:52.274
the system where more money gives an advantage!

675
37:52.341 --> 37:53.476
Nice!

676
37:55.845 --> 37:58.848
Please give me your vote!

677
37:58.914 --> 38:01.951
Thank you, thank you.

678
38:02.551 --> 38:04.553
It must be tough in this heat, everyone.

679
38:05.488 --> 38:07.456
Don't push yourselves too hard.

680
38:08.557 --> 38:09.658
Thank you.

681
38:10.926 --> 38:13.195
I left my own district to come here.

682
38:14.730 --> 38:17.032
The things you do for your kids!

683
38:19.802 --> 38:21.437
-Your seat is over there. -Yes.

684
38:22.905 --> 38:24.106
-Sir. -Yeah?

685
38:24.874 --> 38:26.041
Hayate says

686
38:26.642 --> 38:30.246
he wants to decline your support speech.

687
38:30.312 --> 38:31.247
What?

688
38:31.814 --> 38:34.617
He doesn't want favoritism between siblings.

689
38:35.418 --> 38:37.353
What is he thinking?

690
38:39.188 --> 38:41.157
He's the endorsed candidate!

691
38:41.223 --> 38:42.758
Why would he do that?

692
38:42.825 --> 38:46.328
If he gets both money and a speech too,

693
38:46.395 --> 38:48.030
it would be unfair to his sister.

694
38:50.699 --> 38:52.067
The money was stolen.

695
38:54.637 --> 38:56.272
It was never given out.

696
38:58.340 --> 38:59.275
What?

697
38:59.341 --> 39:02.711
And safe and secure disaster prevention!

698
39:05.981 --> 39:08.551
With these three pillars,

699
39:08.617 --> 39:11.353
I'll work as a member of the Kokuji Party

700
39:11.420 --> 39:16.392
to create a new, stronger Nipponia, that will stand its ground!

701
39:21.130 --> 39:23.566
I'll talk to him directly. Where is he now?

702
39:24.867 --> 39:28.037
Sir! There's a new article. Bribery suspicion.

703
39:30.139 --> 39:32.141
SUSPICION OF ELECTION BRIBERY IN CHIBA 17?

704
39:32.208 --> 39:35.010
DID THE BROTHER FAIL TO BUY VOTES?

705
39:51.527 --> 39:54.997
Three days before the vote, an article suspecting bribery came out.

706
39:55.064 --> 39:58.033
Do you think it affected voters?

707
39:58.100 --> 39:59.802
As a matter of fact,

708
40:00.836 --> 40:03.806
I can say I committed no such crime.

709
40:04.773 --> 40:06.342
On top of that, the reason I lost,

710
40:07.142 --> 40:09.311
perhaps, is because I was a candidate

711
40:09.979 --> 40:11.780
without my own opinions.

712
40:13.949 --> 40:17.453
I got a seat through proportional representation. So…

713
40:17.520 --> 40:21.090
I'll rethink what kind of politician I want to be.

714
40:21.156 --> 40:23.459
Independent newcomer Miyabi Kobayakawa

715
40:23.526 --> 40:27.196
defeated Kokuji Party newcomer Hayate Kobayakawa by 210 votes.

716
40:27.263 --> 40:30.566
You have won this first battle. Can you tell us your thoughts?

717
40:31.066 --> 40:33.102
English is fine too.

718
40:33.168 --> 40:34.637
Maybe next time.

719
40:36.972 --> 40:38.340
First,

720
40:38.407 --> 40:42.311
I apologize to Mr. Hachimaki, who ran in the same district.

721
40:42.378 --> 40:44.013
-Mr. Hachimaki? -Yes.

722
40:44.580 --> 40:45.915
She's apologizing.

723
40:48.217 --> 40:51.787
Our sibling uproar probably got in his way.

724
40:52.588 --> 40:53.622
I'm sorry.

725
40:53.689 --> 40:54.857
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA - CHIBA 17

726
40:55.524 --> 40:57.660
People talk about winning and losing,

727
40:57.726 --> 41:00.763
but democracy isn't just majority rule.

728
41:01.430 --> 41:03.532
It's not about winning or losing. Right?

729
41:04.033 --> 41:05.467
What matters is

730
41:06.068 --> 41:09.238
finding a happiness everyone can share,

731
41:09.305 --> 41:12.608
and elections are the process for it.

732
41:14.577 --> 41:18.013
I've become the representative of District 17.

733
41:18.681 --> 41:20.916
Not only for those who voted for me,

734
41:20.983 --> 41:23.018
but for everyone who voted,

735
41:23.085 --> 41:26.789
including those who voted for Mr. Hachimaki.

736
41:26.855 --> 41:28.223
I'll honor all your wishes,

737
41:28.290 --> 41:29.592
as much as I can,

738
41:30.225 --> 41:31.760
as I go into national politics.

739
41:32.494 --> 41:33.896
Thank you.

740
42:01.757 --> 42:03.459
Congratulations.

741
42:05.060 --> 42:05.828
Here.

742
42:07.096 --> 42:08.597
A little gift.

743
42:08.664 --> 42:09.498
Huh?

744
42:10.332 --> 42:11.433
Are you sure?

745
42:11.500 --> 42:13.535
I got a mountain of them.

746
42:14.370 --> 42:15.571
I would throw it away.

747
42:18.474 --> 42:19.508
If I…

748
42:20.209 --> 42:21.777
should leave the house…

749
42:21.844 --> 42:24.046
What are you saying? It's fine.

750
42:24.113 --> 42:26.415
You can just live there. It's close by too.

751
42:29.551 --> 42:30.953
More importantly,

752
42:32.321 --> 42:33.756
I have a proposal for you.

753
42:36.892 --> 42:38.761
Join the Kokuji Party.

754
42:49.004 --> 42:50.305
Mr. Natsume.

755
42:50.372 --> 42:52.408
I came to greet you.

756
42:52.474 --> 42:53.776
SECRETARY YAYOI KISARAGI

757
42:53.842 --> 42:56.178
Secretary? Weren't you an election consultant?

758
42:56.245 --> 42:58.847
I quit that and became Miyabi's secretary.

759
42:59.715 --> 43:01.016
I see.

760
43:01.650 --> 43:03.285
We won.

761
43:03.352 --> 43:07.156
Who would have thought she would win just by being able to speak English?

762
43:07.222 --> 43:08.424
Just?

763
43:09.358 --> 43:11.093
Our Miyabi

764
43:11.160 --> 43:13.996
looked more like a new wind to the voters, I guess.

765
43:16.398 --> 43:17.900
By the way…

766
43:18.901 --> 43:21.870
Does the safe in the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office

767
43:21.937 --> 43:24.606
also hold losing lottery tickets?

768
43:25.841 --> 43:27.409
Well, I don't know.

769
43:28.544 --> 43:30.612
I'm glad we had a fair fight.

770
43:34.516 --> 43:36.685
We should thank the great thief.

771
43:43.559 --> 43:46.095
I hope to see you again.

772
43:47.896 --> 43:49.098
Likewise.

773
44:02.144 --> 44:03.078
Next episode!

774
44:03.145 --> 44:06.648
A storm of fake news and malicious comments ravages the Internet!

775
44:06.715 --> 44:10.252
Tracing the source reveals how money controls the system.

776
44:10.319 --> 44:14.123
If you can make money writing lies online, you would do it, right?

777
44:14.189 --> 44:15.023
Would you do it?

778
44:15.090 --> 44:15.924
You wouldn't?

779
44:15.991 --> 44:17.025
I wouldn't.

780
44:17.092 --> 44:20.129
Are you okay, Nipponia? Hang in there, Nipponia!

781
44:20.195 --> 44:22.097
The bait has been thrown in.

782
44:22.164 --> 44:24.700
Now who will be caught by it?!

783
44:25.200 --> 44:28.537
I'm actually pretty angry.

784
44:28.604 --> 44:30.072
Subtitle translation by: Quang N.N.
